      "message": "additional option gives no benefit (icmp flow hash) for the users by default, but forces all of them to pay the tax with additional checks.\n\n```\nif (PREDICT_TRUE(is_tcp_udp)) // gives the hint to handle the math traffic path almost w/o perfomance impact\n  {\n    t1 \u003d tcp-\u003esrc;\n    t2 \u003d tcp-\u003edst;\n  }\nelse\n  t1 \u003d t2 \u003d is_icmp_echo ? echo-\u003eid : 0; // reuses original fast cmov with constant instead of additional branching.\n```\n\nwith this idea almost unavoidable per-packet cost gives benefit in return - balancing for the rest of protocols, so I\u0027m afraid opt-in just steals perf here.\ndouble cmov although will give double latency due one cmov dependency on the second, so better not be used.",
